From 7edb579b562d67e6488d67690d6cf9fa5942d430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:16:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] S1-60: api-received-credits (L-150)

The recipientId search, and with it /wallets/{id}/transactions/received,
now matches only transactions that credit the address: a top-level
recipientId, or a Core/6 transfer with an item paid to the address. It no
longer matches delegate registrations sent by the address.

The broader address filter is or(senderId, recipientId), so it still finds
a wallet's own delegate registration through its senderId clause. The
transaction handlers never query by recipientId or address, so the change
is API only.

Test: patches/tests/60-api-received-credits.test.js (fails on b45369d7,
passes with this patch).

Patch: 60
Ledger: L-150
Consensus: no
---
